# .gitignore for the public story repo (working name: byte-by-byte)
#
# This repo holds PROSE, SANITISED TOOLING and AGGREGATE NUMBERS.
# Rule of thumb: if it is game code, somebody else's upload, a credential, or a binary,
# it does not belong here. Every block below is a thing that would either be illegal to
# publish, unsafe to publish, or simply too big to belong in git.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. the game, and anything built from it
# Nothing shipped by Bethesda, nothing generated out of the image.
*.exe
*.dll
*.asi
*.esp
*.esm
*.bsa
*.ba2
*.sav
*.nif
*.kf
*.dds
*.wav
*.ogg
Fallout3.exe
FalloutNV.exe
*.obj
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.map
*.bin
*.dat
*.asm              # machine listings are derived from the game image

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2. decompiled / harvested source
# Never public: our candidates, the rival drafts the service served us, the working tree.
claims/
rivals/
out/
decompiled/
functions/
unit_*.cpp
cand*.cpp
best.cpp
match_*.cpp
*.orig.cpp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. credentials and claim records
# The API key, the packets (they carry signed download URLs) and the claim ledger.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*f3decomp_key*
_claims.json
packet.json
pack.tar.gz
secrets*
credentials*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4. compiler, SDKs, images
vs2005/
wine-vs2005/
SDK/
*.iso
*.msi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5. build, scratch, caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
*.log
*.tmp
tmp/
temp/
scratchpad/
work*/
variants*/
*.tmp.*
.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6. editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 7. big derived data: publish aggregates, not dumps
# The story needs numbers (yield per band, ndiff histograms, twin coverage), not the raw
# 20 MB indexes. Commit those as small CSV/Markdown tables under data/.
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.sqlite
*.db
*.jsonl
twins/cache/
_condensed.json
_twin_by_unit.json
_index.json
*nul

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 8. keep these, even though a rule above is broad
# Aggregate tables and the sanitised tools are the point of the repo.
!data/*.csv
!data/*.md
!tools/**
!chapters/**
!lessons/**
!candidates/**
